{"data":{"id":"10.48550/arxiv.2605.15455","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2605.15455","prefix":"10.48550","suffix":"arxiv.2605.15455","identifiers":[{"identifier":"2605.15455","identifierType":"arXiv"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"alternateIdentifierType":"arXiv","alternateIdentifier":"2605.15455"}],"creators":[{"name":"Karny, Sheer","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Sheer","familyName":"Karny","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Baez, Anthony","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Anthony","familyName":"Baez","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Pataranutaporn, Pat","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Pat","familyName":"Pataranutaporn","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]}],"titles":[{"title":"Surfacing Neural Activations Over Multi-Turn Conversation Improves User Calibration to LLM Behavioral Drift"}],"publisher":"arXiv","container":{},"publicationYear":2026,"subjects":[{"lang":"en","subject":"Human-Computer Interaction (cs.HC)","subjectScheme":"arXiv"},{"subject":"FOS: Computer and information sciences","subjectScheme":"Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"}],"contributors":[],"dates":[{"date":"2026-05-14T22:37:56Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2026-05-18T00:12:51Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2026-10-14T18:00:53Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v2"},{"date":"2026-10-16T00:05:38Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v2"},{"date":"2026-05","dateType":"Available","dateInformation":"v1"}],"language":null,"types":{"ris":"GEN","bibtex":"misc","citeproc":"article","schemaOrg":"CreativeWork","resourceType":"Article","resourceTypeGeneral":"Preprint"},"relatedIdentifiers":[],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":[],"formats":[],"version":"2","rightsList":[{"rights":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","rightsUri":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode","schemeUri":"https://spdx.org/licenses/","rightsIdentifier":"cc-by-4.0","rightsIdentifierScheme":"SPDX"}],"descriptions":[{"description":"Current human-AI interaction (HAI) only surfaces model outputs, hiding how LLM behavior can shift unpredictably toward unsafe behaviors in multi-turn conversations, potentially undermining users' goals or wellbeing. To address this harmful opacity in multi-turn HAI, we introduce an interface that surfaces an LLM's internal activations to help users anticipate and evaluate model behavior. We construct behavioral scores from these activations for six HAI-relevant traits using mechanistic interpretability methods, then visualize them via a dynamic sunburst, drift panel, and attentional cues. In a counterbalanced, randomized controlled study (N=246), both static and dynamic transparency interfaces improved participants' anticipation and evaluation performance (d=-0.36) while helping temper overconfidence in their predictive abilities. Furthermore, the multi-turn interface significantly outperformed the static visualization (d=-0.32) while remaining similarly usable. Our findings suggest that continuously surfacing internal model representations to everyday users is a meaningful and tractable step toward continuously transparent and informed HAI.","descriptionType":"Abstract"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"xml":"","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.15455","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":1,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"mds","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"viewsOverTime":[],"downloadCount":0,"downloadsOverTime":[],"referenceCount":0,"citationCount":0,"citationsOverTime":[],"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":0,"versionOfCount":0,"created":"2026-05-18T01:49:44.000Z","registered":"2026-05-18T01:49:44.000Z","published":"2026","updated":"2026-10-16T03:19:31.000Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"data":{"id":"arxiv.content","type":"clients"}},"provider":{"data":{"id":"arxiv","type":"providers"}},"media":{"data":{"id":"10.48550/arxiv.2605.15455","type":"me